/-!
# Relative property (T) for `(ℤ² ⋊ G, ℤ²)`

For a group `G` acting on `ℤ²` through an injective homomorphism `ψ : G →* SL(2, ℤ)`, the normal
subgroup `ℤ²` in the semidirect product `ℤ² ⋊ G` has relative property (T) if and only if `G` does
not have Følner sets (equivalently, is not amenable as a discrete group). In particular, since
`SL(2, ℤ)` contains Sanov's rank-two free subgroup generated by `[[1, 2], [0, 1]]` and
`[[1, 0], [2, 1]]`, the pair `(ℤ² ⋊ SL(2, ℤ), ℤ²)` has relative property (T) (Kazhdan, Margulis),
as does `(ℤ² ⋊ F₂, ℤ²)` for Sanov's free subgroup, whereas for the upper unipotent shear subgroup
`{[[1, n], [0, 1]] : n ∈ ℤ}` relative property (T) fails.

The proof of Burger's criterion uses the spectral measure of the restriction of a unitary
representation `ρ` of `ℤ² ⋊ G` to `ℤ²`, which is a projection-valued measure `P` on the Pontryagin
dual torus `𝕋²` satisfying `G`-equivariance
(`ContRepresentation.map_diag_spectralPVM_restrict_inl_apply_inr`).
When `ρ` has no nonzero `ℤ²`-invariant vector, the trivial character `{1} ⊆ 𝕋²` has zero spectral
mass. Using principal-branch angular coordinates `coord : 𝕋² → (-π, π]²` and radial projection to
the real projective line `ℙ ℝ (Fin 2 → ℝ)`, the pushforwards `ν_ξ` of the diagonal spectral
measures `P.diag ξ` of almost invariant unit vectors `ξ` form a net of Borel probability measures
on the compact space `ℙ ℝ (Fin 2 → ℝ)`. Near `1 ∈ 𝕋²` the map `coord` intertwines the dual action
of `g ∈ SL(2, ℤ)` with multiplication by `gᵀ`, while away from `1` the spectral mass of `P.diag ξ`
is controlled by the displacements of `ξ` under the two standard generators of `ℤ²`. Any weak-star
cluster point of `(ν_ξ)` is therefore invariant under the contragredient projective action of `G`,
which forces `G` to have Følner sets by Furstenberg's lemma
(`TauCeti.hasFoelnerSets_of_injective_gl_int_of_map_smul_projectivization_eq`). Conversely, when
`G` has Følner sets, so does the extension `ℤ² ⋊ G`, and the counting-measure left regular
representation obstructs relative property (T) (`Subgroup.not_relativePropertyT_of_hasFoelnerSets`).

## Main results

* `TauCeti.not_amenable_slTwo`, `TauCeti.not_hasFoelnerSets_slTwo`: `SL(2, ℤ)` is not amenable.
* `Subgroup.relativePropertyT_inl_of_not_hasFoelnerSets`,
  `Subgroup.relativePropertyT_inl_iff_not_hasFoelnerSets`,
  `Subgroup.relativePropertyT_inl_of_not_amenable`,
  `Subgroup.relativePropertyT_inl_iff_not_amenable`: **Burger's theorem** characterizing relative
  property (T) of `(ℤ² ⋊ G, ℤ²)` for any group `G` embedding in `SL(2, ℤ)`.
* `Subgroup.relativePropertyT_inl_slTwoAction_of_not_hasFoelnerSets`,
  `Subgroup.relativePropertyT_inl_slTwoAction_iff_not_hasFoelnerSets`,
  `Subgroup.relativePropertyT_inl_slTwoAction_of_not_amenable`,
  `Subgroup.relativePropertyT_inl_slTwoAction_iff_not_amenable`: specialization to subgroups
  `G : Subgroup SL(2, ℤ)`.
* `Subgroup.relativePropertyT_inl_slTwo`: **Kazhdan–Margulis theorem**, `(ℤ² ⋊ SL(2, ℤ), ℤ²)` has
  relative property (T).
* `Subgroup.relativePropertyT_inl_freeGroup_slTwo`: relative property (T) for `(ℤ² ⋊ F₂, ℤ²)` via
  Sanov's embedding.
* `Subgroup.not_relativePropertyT_inl_transvectionHom_range`: failure of relative property (T) for
  the upper unipotent shear subgroup `{[[1, n], [0, 1]] : n ∈ ℤ}`.

The relative property (T) theorems live in the root `Subgroup` namespace to match
`Subgroup.RelativePropertyT` and support dot notation on `G : Subgroup SL(2, ℤ)`.

## References

* D. A. Kazhdan, *On the connection of the dual space of a group with the structure of its closed
  subgroups*, Funct. Anal. Appl. 1 (1967), 63–65.
* G. A. Margulis, *Finitely-additive invariant measures on Euclidean spaces*, Ergodic Theory Dynam.
  Systems 2 (1982), 383–396.
* M. Burger, *Kazhdan constants for `SL(3, ℤ)`*, J. Reine Angew. Math. 413 (1991), 36–67.
* B. Bekka, P. de la Harpe and A. Valette, *Kazhdan's Property (T)*, Cambridge University Press
  (2008), Example 1.7.4 and Proposition 4.2.5.
* C. Anantharaman and S. Popa, *An Introduction to II₁ Factors*, Example 14.2.8.
-/

